  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:protocol-compatibility",
  "domain": "distributed-systems",
  "definition": "Protocol compatibility is the property that two or more implementations of a communication protocol can correctly exchange messages and interpret them consistently, whether they are identical versions or different versions designed to interwork. It requires agreement on message framing, semantics, and versioning strategy, often achieved through published technical standards. Protocol compatibility is a precondition for interoperability between independently developed systems.",
